# SuperFrontierLiquid full-universe genesis.
#
# This file declares the complete tradable universe of `docs/PLAN.md` §3:
#
#   Class   Underlyings              Instruments
#   ------  -----------------------  ----------------------------
#   Crypto  BTC, ETH, SOL            spot, perpetual, dated future
#   Equity  AAPL, TSLA, NVDA, SPY    spot, perpetual
#
# `genesis.jsonl` and `genesis-perps.jsonl` remain as they were and are pinned
# by their own tests; this is a third, wider chain configuration, not a
# replacement for either.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ORDER OF THE `perp_market` AND `future_market` LINES IS CONSENSUS DATA.
#
# The Nth `perp_market` line becomes `DerivId::perp(N)`, the Nth `future_market`
# line becomes `DerivId::future(N)`, and those identifiers are what every stored
# position, order and oracle update refers to. Reordering a line silently
# repoints every position on the chain at a different contract.
#
# The order below matches `cb_types::symbols::PERPS` and `::FUTURES` exactly,
# and `cb-genesis/tests/full_genesis.rs` asserts that it does — including the
# risk parameters on each line. If you add or move a market here, that test
# tells you what else has to move with it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `${VAR}` tokens are substituted from the environment before JSON parsing; a
# sibling `.env` file is auto-loaded and real env vars win. See
# `crates/cb-genesis/src/spec.rs` for the substitution rules.
#
# Required env vars:
#   MYCHAINID          chain ID (u32). 1 = mainnet, 2 = testnet.
#   MYDENOM            native denom string (e.g. "ULD"). Display-only; the
#                      quote asset is `AssetId::Usd` regardless.
#   MYWALLET0..2       validator wallets (leader rotation follows line order).
#   MYWALLET3          community wallet.
#   INITIAL_AMOUNT     starting USD credit per validator wallet, micro-USD.
#   ORACLE_AUTHORITY   the sole address allowed to sign `OracleUpdate` for
#                      every market on this chain.
#   DEMO_TRADER0..2    demo traders pre-funded with margin collateral.
#
# On ORACLE_AUTHORITY being a single key: `genesis-perps.jsonl` deliberately
# splits the oracle role per market so one compromised key cannot tip two feeds.
# This file uses one authority instead, because the simulator runs one price
# service that publishes all eleven feeds and splitting it would mean operating
# eleven keys for no isolation that anyone would actually get. A production
# deployment should go back to per-market authorities.
{"kind":"chain","chain_id":${MYCHAINID},"denom":"${MYDENOM}","insurance_fund_seed":"5000000000000"}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Validators. Line order is leader-rotation order; validators[0] proposes view 0.
{"kind":"validator","seed":"cb-validator-0","wallet":"${MYWALLET0}","weight":1,"initial_amount":"${INITIAL_AMOUNT}"}
{"kind":"validator","seed":"cb-validator-1","wallet":"${MYWALLET1}","weight":1,"initial_amount":"${INITIAL_AMOUNT}"}
{"kind":"validator","seed":"cb-validator-2","wallet":"${MYWALLET2}","weight":1,"initial_amount":"${INITIAL_AMOUNT}"}
{"kind":"validator","seed":"cb-validator-3","wallet":"${MYWALLET3}","weight":1,"initial_amount":"${INITIAL_AMOUNT}"}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPOT MARKETS
#
# `min_qty` is in the base asset's own base units (`AssetId::decimals()`), and
# `tick_size` is in wire-price units. The wire price scale is NOT the same on
# every market: it is `10^(quote_decimals + 8 - base_decimals)` — see
# `cb_types::scales::spot_price_scale_exp`. Concretely:
#
#   BTC/USD     10^6 per $1   (BTC has 8 decimals)
#   SOL/USD     10^5 per $1   (SOL has 9)
#   AAPL & co.  10^8 per $1   (equities have 6, same as USD)
#
# So a `tick_size` of 100000 is ten cents on BTC, and 1000000 is one cent on an
# equity. They are different numbers for the same reason the assets have
# different decimals, which is why this is spelled out per line below.
{"kind":"market","id":"btc_usd","base":"btc","quote":"usd","tick_size":100000,"min_qty":1000,"fee_bps":10}
# ETH/USD is the one market whose wire price scale is degenerate: 18 base
# decimals against the executor's fixed 1e8 notional divisor gives a negative
# exponent, so one whole ETH costs less than one wire-price unit and no human
# price can be represented (`ScaleError::SubUnitPriceScale`). ETH's decimals are
# frozen in consensus state and cannot be revisited, so this market keeps the
# unit tick/lot the older genesis files use. It trades in raw integers; the
# perpetual below is the usable way to take ETH exposure.
{"kind":"market","id":"eth_usd","base":"eth","quote":"usd","tick_size":1,"min_qty":1,"fee_bps":10}
# SOL/USD: tick 1000 = $0.01, min_qty 1000000 lamports = 0.001 SOL.
{"kind":"market","id":"sol_usd","base":"sol","quote":"usd","tick_size":1000,"min_qty":1000000,"fee_bps":10}
# Equity spot. tick 1000000 = $0.01, the conventional penny increment.
# min_qty 10000 = 0.01 share: fine enough for fractional-share trading, coarse
# enough that a quantity computed at the wrong decimal scale fails the lot check
# instead of executing 100x too large. Every equity gets identical parameters —
# a uniform tier is one less thing for a trader to get wrong.
{"kind":"market","id":"aapl_usd","base":"aapl","quote":"usd","tick_size":1000000,"min_qty":10000,"fee_bps":10}
{"kind":"market","id":"tsla_usd","base":"tsla","quote":"usd","tick_size":1000000,"min_qty":10000,"fee_bps":10}
{"kind":"market","id":"nvda_usd","base":"nvda","quote":"usd","tick_size":1000000,"min_qty":10000,"fee_bps":10}
{"kind":"market","id":"spy_usd","base":"spy","quote":"usd","tick_size":1000000,"min_qty":10000,"fee_bps":10}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PERPETUAL MARKETS — line order maps to DerivId::perp(N).
#
#   0 BTC-PERP   50x     4 TSLA-PERP  5x
#   1 ETH-PERP   25x     5 NVDA-PERP  5x
#   2 SOL-PERP   20x     6 SPY-PERP   5x
#   3 AAPL-PERP  5x
#
# Indices 0 and 1 match `genesis.jsonl` / `genesis-perps.jsonl` so tooling and
# stored state stay compatible across all three configurations.
#
# `tick_size` and `lot_size` are at the q8 price scale and the fixed 1e8
# contract-quantity scale respectively. NOTE that `lot_size` is in CONTRACT
# units (1e8 per whole underlying, the same for every market), not in the
# underlying's spot base units — for an equity those differ by 100x. See
# `cb_types::scales`.
#
# Margin: `initial_margin_bps` is the reciprocal of the leverage cap and
# `maintenance_margin_bps` is half of it, asserted by
# `cb_types::symbols`'s `risk_params_are_internally_consistent`. Leverage tiers
# and the reasoning behind each cap are documented on `cb_types::symbols::PERPS`.
#
# Execution enforces these per-market risk limits. The default piecewise
# leverage tiers remain an additional floor; the stricter requirement wins
# separately for each market, before summing the portfolio requirement.
{"kind":"perp_market","id":"btc_perp","underlying":"btc","tick_size":"100","lot_size":"1000","max_leverage_x100":5000,"initial_margin_bps":200,"maintenance_margin_bps":100,"taker_fee_bps":3,"maker_fee_bps_signed":-1,"funding_interval_blocks":3600,"funding_rate_cap_q9":1000000,"oracle_authority":"${ORACLE_AUTHORITY}","max_position_notional":"100000000000000","paused":false}
{"kind":"perp_market","id":"eth_perp","underlying":"eth","tick_size":"100","lot_size":"1000","max_leverage_x100":2500,"initial_margin_bps":400,"maintenance_margin_bps":200,"taker_fee_bps":3,"maker_fee_bps_signed":-1,"funding_interval_blocks":3600,"funding_rate_cap_q9":1000000,"oracle_authority":"${ORACLE_AUTHORITY}","max_position_notional":"50000000000000","paused":false}
{"kind":"perp_market","id":"sol_perp","underlying":"sol","tick_size":"100","lot_size":"1000","max_leverage_x100":2000,"initial_margin_bps":500,"maintenance_margin_bps":250,"taker_fee_bps":3,"maker_fee_bps_signed":-1,"funding_interval_blocks":3600,"funding_rate_cap_q9":1000000,"oracle_authority":"${ORACLE_AUTHORITY}","max_position_notional":"20000000000000","paused":false}
# Equity perpetuals. Cash-settled against a mocked reference price; nothing
# settles into a real share and no dividend or corporate action is modelled.
#
# Three parameters differ from the crypto perps above, all for the same
# underlying reason — a synthetic equity has no arbitrage path back to a real
# share, and the real thing gaps on news:
#   * 5x cap / 20% IM / 10% MM, so a position survives an earnings-sized gap.
#   * tick 1000000 = $0.01 at the q8 scale, matching the equity spot tick.
#   * funding_rate_cap_q9 doubled to 2000000. Funding is the only force pulling
#     the contract back toward the reference price, and with no arbitrageur able
#     to deliver the underlying it has to do that work alone.
# max_position_notional is $5M, well below BTC's $100M: these books are the
# thinnest on the venue and a position has to be closable into them.
{"kind":"perp_market","id":"aapl_perp","underlying":"aapl","tick_size":"1000000","lot_size":"1000000","max_leverage_x100":500,"initial_margin_bps":2000,"maintenance_margin_bps":1000,"taker_fee_bps":3,"maker_fee_bps_signed":-1,"funding_interval_blocks":3600,"funding_rate_cap_q9":2000000,"oracle_authority":"${ORACLE_AUTHORITY}","max_position_notional":"5000000000000","paused":false}
{"kind":"perp_market","id":"tsla_perp","underlying":"tsla","tick_size":"1000000","lot_size":"1000000","max_leverage_x100":500,"initial_margin_bps":2000,"maintenance_margin_bps":1000,"taker_fee_bps":3,"maker_fee_bps_signed":-1,"funding_interval_blocks":3600,"funding_rate_cap_q9":2000000,"oracle_authority":"${ORACLE_AUTHORITY}","max_position_notional":"5000000000000","paused":false}
{"kind":"perp_market","id":"nvda_perp","underlying":"nvda","tick_size":"1000000","lot_size":"1000000","max_leverage_x100":500,"initial_margin_bps":2000,"maintenance_margin_bps":1000,"taker_fee_bps":3,"maker_fee_bps_signed":-1,"funding_interval_blocks":3600,"funding_rate_cap_q9":2000000,"oracle_authority":"${ORACLE_AUTHORITY}","max_position_notional":"5000000000000","paused":false}
{"kind":"perp_market","id":"spy_perp","underlying":"spy","tick_size":"1000000","lot_size":"1000000","max_leverage_x100":500,"initial_margin_bps":2000,"maintenance_margin_bps":1000,"taker_fee_bps":3,"maker_fee_bps_signed":-1,"funding_interval_blocks":3600,"funding_rate_cap_q9":2000000,"oracle_authority":"${ORACLE_AUTHORITY}","max_position_notional":"5000000000000","paused":false}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATED FUTURES — line order maps to DerivId::future(N).
#
#   0 ETH-260626  ~90 days   10x
#   1 BTC-261225  ~180 days  25x
#   2 SOL-270326  ~270 days  10x
#
# Crypto only; equities list spot and perpetual only, per `docs/PLAN.md` §3.
# Index 0 is an ETH contract to match both older genesis files.
#
# Each carries roughly half the leverage of the perpetual on the same
# underlying: a dated contract is exposed to basis that need not converge until
# expiry and can widen sharply near it, which a perpetual's continuously
# converging mark does not have.
#
# `expiry_height` is a BLOCK HEIGHT, not a date. The `YYMMDD` in the symbol is a
# nominal label and nothing derives one from the other — block time is a
# deployment property, so a chain booted late would have every derived date
# quietly wrong. Heights below are ~90 / ~180 / ~270 days at one-second blocks,
# spaced so they expire in the same order their labels suggest and far enough
# out that a dev cluster never races expiry.
#
# `settlement_method` 0 = TWAP over the last `settlement_window_blocks` mark
# snapshots (1800 blocks ~ 30 minutes), which is harder to manipulate at the
# settlement instant than method 1's single oracle read.
{"kind":"future_market","id":"eth_260626","underlying":"eth","tick_size":"100","lot_size":"1000","max_leverage_x100":1000,"initial_margin_bps":1000,"maintenance_margin_bps":500,"taker_fee_bps":3,"maker_fee_bps_signed":-1,"expiry_height":7776000,"settlement_method":0,"settlement_window_blocks":1800,"oracle_authority":"${ORACLE_AUTHORITY}","paused":false}
{"kind":"future_market","id":"btc_261225","underlying":"btc","tick_size":"100","lot_size":"1000","max_leverage_x100":2500,"initial_margin_bps":400,"maintenance_margin_bps":200,"taker_fee_bps":3,"maker_fee_bps_signed":-1,"expiry_height":15552000,"settlement_method":0,"settlement_window_blocks":1800,"oracle_authority":"${ORACLE_AUTHORITY}","paused":false}
{"kind":"future_market","id":"sol_270326","underlying":"sol","tick_size":"100","lot_size":"1000","max_leverage_x100":1000,"initial_margin_bps":1000,"maintenance_margin_bps":500,"taker_fee_bps":3,"maker_fee_bps_signed":-1,"expiry_height":23328000,"settlement_method":0,"settlement_window_blocks":1800,"oracle_authority":"${ORACLE_AUTHORITY}","paused":false}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo margin accounts. `AdjustMargin` is not a supported tx in v1, so any
# address that wants to place a perp order on a fresh chain MUST be seeded here.
# $10M each (micro-USD) — enough to hold a position on every market at once,
# including the 20% initial margin an equity perp declares.
{"kind":"margin_account","address":"${DEMO_TRADER0}","collateral":"10000000000000"}
{"kind":"margin_account","address":"${DEMO_TRADER1}","collateral":"10000000000000"}
{"kind":"margin_account","address":"${DEMO_TRADER2}","collateral":"10000000000000"}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Treasury and community wallet. Balances are per-asset base units, so the same
# human quantity is a different integer on each line: 1000 BTC is 1e11 (8
# decimals), 10000 ETH is 1e22 (18), 10000 SOL is 1e13 (9), and 100000 shares of
# an equity is 1e11 (6). Getting one of these wrong by a factor of ten is the
# single easiest mistake to make in this file.
{"kind":"company","address":"${TREASURY}","balances":{"btc":"100000000000","eth":"10000000000000000000000","sol":"10000000000000","usd":"100000000000000","aapl":"100000000000","tsla":"100000000000","nvda":"100000000000","spy":"100000000000"}}
{"kind":"community_wallet","address":"${MYWALLET3}","balances":{"usd":"${INITIAL_AMOUNT}"}}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Seeded simulation accounts. 64 deterministic traders derived from
# `keccak256(seed_prefix || i)`, each funded on every asset so a bot can quote
# both sides of any market in the universe without a faucet round-trip.
#
# Per trader: 100 BTC, 1000 ETH, 1000 SOL, $10M, and 1000 shares of each equity.
{"kind":"sim","num_traders":64,"seed_prefix":"cb-sim-trader-","balances":{"btc":"10000000000","eth":"1000000000000000000000","sol":"1000000000000","usd":"10000000000000","aapl":"1000000000","tsla":"1000000000","nvda":"1000000000","spy":"1000000000"}}
